U.S. SEC again extends deadline for private funds’ enhanced risk-data reporting

The SEC has extended for the second time the deadline by which private investment funds must comply with new enhanced disclosure rules. These rules require reporting confidentially detailed information on exposures (investments, counterparties, currencies, industries, etc.). 
Reuters

New deadline: October 1, 2026. 
Reuters

Implication: regulators are trying to get ahead of systemic risks, but fund managers are pushing back on the burden / timing. This could affect fund structuring, compliance costs, and how private funds allocate resources to risk monitoring. 
Reuters

