“Private markets exposure rising at top pension funds”

A Bloomberg piece noted that large pension funds are increasing their allocations to private assets. 
Bloomberg

While not a regulatory action, this carries potential systemic risk if valuations, liquidity, or risk disclosure do not keep pace. Regulators would likely monitor this because large unhedged exposures across pension systems can amplify shocks. 
